-07-23"}]},"company":{"attrs":{"cik":320187,"company":"Nike","fy_end":"2015-05-31","activeRevision":"2f331a24d239","liveRevision":""}},"filings":[{"attrs":{"accn":"0000320187-14-000097","filed":"2014-07-25","cik":320187,"company":"Nike","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320187/000032018714000097/0000320187-14-000097-index.htm","form":"10-K"}},{"attrs":{"accn":"0000320187-15-000113","filed":"2015-07-23","cik":320187,"company":"Nike","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320187/000032018715000113/nke-5312015x10k.htm","form":"10-K"}}],"findings":[],"rulings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"320187_2015-05-31","revisionId":"2f331a24d239","sampleIndex":0,"rulingIndex":3,"finding_index":3,"ruling":"unverified","reason":"Management provides no explicit explanation for the receivables decline or CFO surge (E32-E43). The investigator infers consistency with DTC mix shift and improved collections (lower DSO per E25, E27-E30), but this causal attribution is not management's explanation and the DTC driver is not verified in the numbers (per Finding 0). The Beneish M-score (E31) shows no manipulation, but does not confirm the driver.","evidence":["E25","E26","E27","E28","E29","E30","E31","E38"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":3,"innocent_explanation":"The receivables decline and outsized CFO increase are fully explained by the improving collections trajectory visible in the quarterly DSO data (E27-E30) and the overall DSO improvement from 45 to 40 days (E25), which are reported numbers; the Beneish M-score of -2.80 (E31) further indicates no earnings manipulation. While management does not explicitly quantify the working capital drivers, the numerical pattern itself—lower DSO, higher CFO, lower receivables amid revenue growth—is internally consistent and requires no non-recurring items.","evidence":["E25","E26","E27","E28","E29","E30","E31"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation unverified","confidence":0.85}}],"audit":[{"seq":31,"actor":"evidence-pack","summar